    "long_instructions": "UX Designers often test web apps from the perspective of a specific user so they can identify what works well and what parts are hard for certain users to navigate or use.\r\n\r\nAs a UX Designer, you want to conduct the following test task:\r\n\r\n1. Find one dog that is:\r\n   - Under 2 years old\r\n   - Good with kids\r\n   - Small\r\n2. Open Details to confirm they've found an appropriate dog.\r\n3. Click Adopt.\r\n\r\n## Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Complete the test task from your selected user's perspective.\r\n2. Complete **Part 2: Usability Checklist** on your [activity guide](https://docs.google.com/document/d/1ZJ1TXv9EEma3mcTE9wVZy1fbiKxrlV8qy9Xb9lSl7xE/edit?usp=sharing) based on your experience.\r\n",
    "ai_tutor_prompt_settings": {
      "answerTypes": [
        "ask"
      ],
      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
      }
    },
    "teacher_markdown": "- **Require students to stay in character.**  \r\nStudents must complete the task from their assigned user’s perspective, not their own. Listen for profile-based reasoning rather than personal preference.\r\n\r\n- **Push for evidence from the interface.**\r\nWhen students complete the checklist, require them to reference specific parts of the app (text size, layout, button placement, density of information).\r\n\r\n- **Probe surface-level answers.**\r\nIf a student says “It was confusing,” ask: “Confusing for who?” and “What specifically caused that?” Push them to tie each response back to a user need.\r\n\r\n- **Watch for task breakdown points.**\r\nNotice where students hesitate: scanning the cards, locating age, confirming size, opening Details, or clicking Adopt. These friction points often reveal usability gaps.\r\n\r\n- **Reinforce that usability depends on context.**\r\nIf one student says the app was fine and another says it was difficult, highlight that both can be correct depending on the user profile.\r\n\r\n- **Encourage specific improvement suggestions.**\r\nWhen students propose changes, require them to complete the sentence: “This would help _ because _.”",
    "offer_browser_tts": "false",
    "require_edit_to_continue": "false",
